From: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
Subject: [PATCH] libatomic: Use cache-primed LR/SC on the Gowin AE350

Provide the word compare-exchange primitive for RV32IM builds. The
existing generic libatomic code builds the other operations from it;
sub-word operations retain their masked word-CAS implementations, and
64-bit operations retain the RV32 lock-based implementation.

Both success and failure use full barriers. The strong CAS retries SC
failures and returns the observed value on a comparison failure. A load
and barrier before each LR avoids the AE350 cache-miss limitation.

This patch is applied only by the Gowin AE350 Buildroot profile. Other
RISC-V processors must not select this CPU-specific patch directory.

Signed-off-by: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>

--- /dev/null
+++ b/libatomic/config/riscv/host-config.h
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+/* Gowin AE350 cache-primed atomic operations.
+   Copyright (C) 2026 Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
+
